    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0293" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-02T10:00:00+08:00">July 2, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 2—2:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following message has been sent to Legation, July 2, 9 a.m.: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <list>
                            <item>“1. Through rail traffic Peiping-Mukden resumed yesterday as
                                scheduled. Bomb exploded in a third-class coach of first northbound
                                express at point just north of Tangku killing several Chinese but
                                first through train from Mukden arrived this morning without
                                untoward incident and went on to Peiping.</item>
                            <item>2. Shortly expected further steps in tacit recognition that
                                non-Chinese regime of some permanence exists in Manchuria are
                                effectuation <pb facs="0294" n="204" xml:id="pg204"/> of arrangement
                                for postal relations described in my despatch of June 25<anchor
                                    n="38" xml:id="d166-f1"/> and establishment now definitely
                                planned of five additional Chinese customs stations along the Great
                                Wall mentioned in my despatch June 29<anchor n="38" xml:id="d166-f2"
                                /> as reported under contemplation. While agreement as to postal
                                arrangement is reliably stated to have been reached date of
                                inspection has not been determined. According to authentic
                                information the new customshouses will be set up within 3 weeks
                                under supervision Chinese Commissioner stationed at Peiping who has
                                already arrived in that city for the purpose of
                                organization.”</item>
                        </list>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
